{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-94907","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158725","text":"OpenSentience"}]},{"id":"blk-94908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158726","marks":["bold"],"text":"Open research protocols for machine cognition, structured memory, deliberation topology, and agent governance."}]},{"id":"blk-94909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158727","text":"Published by "},{"id":"spn-158728","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://ampersandboxdesign.com"}],"text":"Ampersand Box Design"},{"id":"spn-158729","text":" under the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-94911","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158730","text":"\"Intelligence is not generation. It is structured accumulation.\""}]}],"id":"blk-94910","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-94912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158731","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Apache%202.0-blue.svg"}],"text":"![License"},{"id":"spn-158732","text":"](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0) "},{"id":"spn-158733","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://img.shields.io/badge/spec-v0.1%20draft-orange.svg"}],"text":"![Spec Status"},{"id":"spn-158734","text":"]() "},{"id":"spn-158735","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://img.shields.io/badge/docs-ReadTheDocs-informational.svg"}],"text":"![Docs"},{"id":"spn-158736","text":"]() "},{"id":"spn-158737","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://img.shields.io/badge/stack-Elixir%20%7C%20OTP-purple.svg"}],"text":"![Stack"},{"id":"spn-158738","text":"]()"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-94914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158739","marks":["bold"],"text":"Re-checked against the tree 2026-08-16."},{"id":"spn-158740","text":" This file had not been touched since 2026-04-12. It said "},{"id":"spn-158741","marks":["bold"],"text":"ten"},{"id":"spn-158742","text":" protocols. There are "},{"id":"spn-158743","marks":["bold"],"text":"twelve"},{"id":"spn-158744","text":" — GRASP and OS-012 SCOPE both landed as drafts and neither reached this page. Graphonomous was listed at v0.3.3 and is "},{"id":"spn-158745","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.4.3"},{"id":"spn-158746","text":". PULSE was listed with five cross-loop tokens and has "},{"id":"spn-158747","marks":["bold"],"text":"six"},{"id":"spn-158748","text":" since v0.1.1.  "},{"id":"spn-158749","marks":["bold"],"text":"The instructive part is how the count was fixed."},{"id":"spn-158750","text":" It was hand-corrected to "},{"id":"spn-158751","marks":["italic"],"text":"eleven"},{"id":"spn-158752","text":" first — from reading the spec directory, which holds an OS-011 file and no OS-012 file — and eleven was still wrong. The right answer came from "},{"id":"spn-158753","marks":["code"],"text":"_rebuild/data/protocols.json"},{"id":"spn-158754","text":", which the "},{"id":"spn-158755","marks":["bold"],"text":"homepage already derives its count from"},{"id":"spn-158756","text":", and which says twelve. So this repository had solved the drift for the page it generates and left the README outside the mechanism. The live site has been saying "},{"id":"spn-158757","marks":["code"],"text":"OS-001 → OS-012"},{"id":"spn-158758","text":" the whole time this file said ten.  "},{"id":"spn-158759","marks":["bold"],"text":"`_rebuild/data/protocols.json` is the source of truth."},{"id":"spn-158760","text":" The table below is hand-maintained and will drift again. Check the JSON.  "},{"id":"spn-158761","marks":["bold"],"text":"The OS-E001 benchmark figures were deliberately left at v0.3.3."},{"id":"spn-158762","text":" That measurement was taken against v0.3.3 and re-labelling it would claim a benchmark nobody ran. A dated result stays dated.  Everything else below was checked and stands."}]}],"id":"blk-94913","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-94915","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158763","text":"What is OpenSentience?"}]},{"id":"blk-94916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158764","text":"OpenSentience is the "},{"id":"spn-158765","marks":["bold"],"text":"research arm"},{"id":"spn-158766","text":" of the [&] Protocol ecosystem. It is "},{"id":"spn-158767","marks":["bold"],"text":"not a product"},{"id":"spn-158768","text":" — it is a research organization that publishes:"}]},{"id":"blk-94917","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-94919","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158769","marks":["bold"],"text":"Twelve numbered protocols"},{"id":"spn-158770","text":" (OS-001 through OS-012) — each defining one cognitive capability or cross-cutting concern, grounded in cognitive science"}]}],"id":"blk-94918","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-94921","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158771","marks":["bold"],"text":"Three runtime artifacts"},{"id":"spn-158772","text":" — a governance shim (OS-006), a benchmark engine (OS-009 PRISM), and a loop manifest standard (OS-010 PULSE)"}]}],"id":"blk-94920","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-94923","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158773","marks":["bold"],"text":"Published research"},{"id":"spn-158774","text":" — cognitive science grounding, empirical benchmarks, and open questions"}]}],"id":"blk-94922","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-94924","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158775","text":"Other [&] portfolio products implement the protocols. OpenSentience defines them, grounds them in theory, and provides the thin enforcement layer that ties them together at runtime."}]},{"id":"blk-94925","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158776","text":"The Twelve Protocols"}]},{"id":"blk-94926","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158777","text":"Eight "},{"id":"spn-158778","marks":["bold"],"text":"cognitive primitives"},{"id":"spn-158779","text":" (OS-001–OS-008), two "},{"id":"spn-158780","marks":["bold"],"text":"cross-cutting protocols"},{"id":"spn-158781","text":" (OS-009, OS-010), one that closes the loop to the world (GRASP), and one for space (OS-012)."}]},{"id":"blk-94927","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158782","marks":["bold"],"text":"This table is hand-maintained and the homepage's is not."},{"id":"spn-158783","text":" "},{"id":"spn-158784","marks":["code"],"text":"_rebuild/data/protocols.json"},{"id":"spn-158785","text":" is the source of truth — the homepage derives its count and range from "},{"id":"spn-158786","marks":["code"],"text":"protocols.length"},{"id":"spn-158787","text":", which is why the site has said twelve while this file said ten. Check the JSON, not this table:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-94929","spans":[{"id":"spn-158788","text":"ID"}]},{"id":"blk-94930","spans":[{"id":"spn-158789","text":"Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-94931","spans":[{"id":"spn-158790","text":"[&] Primitive"}]},{"id":"blk-94932","spans":[{"id":"spn-158791","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-94933","spans":[{"id":"spn-158792","text":"Implementation"}]}],"id":"blk-94928","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-94934","spans":[{"id":"spn-158793","text":"OS-001"}]},{"id":"blk-94935","spans":[{"id":"spn-158794","text":"Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-94936","spans":[{"id":"spn-158795","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"}]},{"id":"blk-94937","spans":[{"id":"spn-158796","text":"v0.4.3 shipped"}]},{"id":"blk-94938","spans":[{"id":"spn-158797","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../graphonomous/"}],"text":"Graphonomous"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94939","spans":[{"id":"spn-158798","text":"OS-002"}]},{"id":"blk-94940","spans":[{"id":"spn-158799","text":"Topological Routing (κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-94941","spans":[{"id":"spn-158800","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.deliberate"}]},{"id":"blk-94942","spans":[{"id":"spn-158801","text":"Spec complete"}]},{"id":"blk-94943","spans":[{"id":"spn-158802","text":"Graphonomous routing layer"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94944","spans":[{"id":"spn-158803","text":"OS-003"}]},{"id":"blk-94945","spans":[{"id":"spn-158804","text":"Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-94946","spans":[{"id":"spn-158805","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.deliberate"}]},{"id":"blk-94947","spans":[{"id":"spn-158806","text":"Spec complete"}]},{"id":"blk-94948","spans":[{"id":"spn-158807","text":"AgenTroMatic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94949","spans":[{"id":"spn-158808","text":"OS-004"}]},{"id":"blk-94950","spans":[{"id":"spn-158809","text":"Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-94951","spans":[{"id":"spn-158810","text":"meta-reasoning"}]},{"id":"blk-94952","spans":[{"id":"spn-158811","text":"Spec complete"}]},{"id":"blk-94953","spans":[{"id":"spn-158812","text":"Graphonomous attention module"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94954","spans":[{"id":"spn-158813","text":"OS-005"}]},{"id":"blk-94955","spans":[{"id":"spn-158814","text":"Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-94956","spans":[{"id":"spn-158815","text":"system"}]},{"id":"blk-94957","spans":[{"id":"spn-158816","text":"Spec complete"}]},{"id":"blk-94958","spans":[{"id":"spn-158817","text":"Graphonomous / Agentelic"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94959","spans":[{"id":"spn-158818","text":"OS-006"}]},{"id":"blk-94960","spans":[{"id":"spn-158819","text":"Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-94961","spans":[{"id":"spn-158820","text":"governance"}]},{"id":"blk-94962","spans":[{"id":"spn-158821","text":"In development"}]},{"id":"blk-94963","spans":[{"id":"spn-158822","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-158823","text":" hex package"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94964","spans":[{"id":"spn-158824","text":"OS-007"}]},{"id":"blk-94965","spans":[{"id":"spn-158825","text":"Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-94966","spans":[{"id":"spn-158826","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.identity"}]},{"id":"blk-94967","spans":[{"id":"spn-158827","text":"Draft"}]},{"id":"blk-94968","spans":[{"id":"spn-158828","text":"OpenSentience security module"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94969","spans":[{"id":"spn-158829","text":"OS-008"}]},{"id":"blk-94970","spans":[{"id":"spn-158830","text":"Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-94971","spans":[{"id":"spn-158831","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.harness"}]},{"id":"blk-94972","spans":[{"id":"spn-158832","text":"Draft"}]},{"id":"blk-94973","spans":[{"id":"spn-158833","text":"OpenSentience harness module"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94974","spans":[{"id":"spn-158834","marks":["bold"],"text":"OS-009"}]},{"id":"blk-94975","spans":[{"id":"spn-158835","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM"},{"id":"spn-158836","text":" (Rating Iterative System Memory)"}]},{"id":"blk-94976","spans":[{"id":"spn-158837","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory + &reason"}]},{"id":"blk-94977","spans":[{"id":"spn-158838","text":"v3.0 in development"}]},{"id":"blk-94978","spans":[{"id":"spn-158839","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../PRISM/"}],"text":"`/PRISM/`"},{"id":"spn-158840","text":" — Fly.io deploy"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94979","spans":[{"id":"spn-158841","marks":["bold"],"text":"OS-010"}]},{"id":"blk-94980","spans":[{"id":"spn-158842","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE"},{"id":"spn-158843","text":" (Uniform Loop State Exchange)"}]},{"id":"blk-94981","spans":[{"id":"spn-158844","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory + &govern + &time"}]},{"id":"blk-94982","spans":[{"id":"spn-158845","text":"v0.1 draft"}]},{"id":"blk-94983","spans":[{"id":"spn-158846","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"../PULSE/"}],"text":"`/PULSE/`"},{"id":"spn-158847","text":" — manifest standard"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94984","spans":[{"id":"spn-158848","text":"OS-011"}]},{"id":"blk-94985","spans":[{"id":"spn-158849","marks":["bold"],"text":"GRASP"},{"id":"spn-158850","text":" (Grounded Readings, Actions and State)"}]},{"id":"blk-94986","spans":[{"id":"spn-158851","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"}]},{"id":"blk-94987","spans":[{"id":"spn-158852","text":"v0.1 draft (2026-04-21)"}]},{"id":"blk-94988","spans":[{"id":"spn-158853","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"}],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-158854","text":" — closes the perception-action gap in OS-001…OS-010"}]}],[{"id":"blk-94989","spans":[{"id":"spn-158855","text":"OS-012"}]},{"id":"blk-94990","spans":[{"id":"spn-158856","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCOPE"},{"id":"spn-158857","text":" (Spatial Claims & Coordination)"}]},{"id":"blk-94991","spans":[{"id":"spn-158858","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.region + &space.claim"}]},{"id":"blk-94992","spans":[{"id":"spn-158859","text":"v0.1 draft"}]},{"id":"blk-94993","spans":[{"id":"spn-158860","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"scope.html"}],"text":"`scope.html`"},{"id":"spn-158861","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-158862","marks":["bold"],"text":"no spec document in `docs/spec/` yet"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-94994","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158863","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-94995","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM (OS-009)  — measures loops over time   diagnostic │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE (OS-010)  — declares loops + signals    temporal  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  OS-001 … OS-008 — cognitive primitives       capability │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&]             — composes capabilities      structural │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-94996","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-94998","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158864","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-158865","text":" composes agents ("},{"id":"spn-158866","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-158867","text":") — structural layer"}]}],"id":"blk-94997","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95000","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158868","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE"},{"id":"spn-158869","text":" gives them a heartbeat ("},{"id":"spn-158870","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-158871","text":") — temporal layer"}]}],"id":"blk-94999","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95002","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158872","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM"},{"id":"spn-158873","text":" measures their effect — diagnostic layer"}]}],"id":"blk-95001","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-95003","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158874","text":"Each protocol is independent. Adoption order is typically [&] → PULSE → PRISM."}]},{"id":"blk-95004","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158875","text":"Protocol Summaries"}]},{"id":"blk-95005","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158876","text":"OS-001: Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-95006","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158877","text":"Hippocampal consolidation-inspired memory. Self-evolving knowledge graph with four node types (episodic, semantic, procedural, temporal), typed/weighted/decaying edges, multi-timescale consolidation, and no model weight modification — all learning is graph-structural."}]},{"id":"blk-95007","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158878","text":"OS-002: Topological Routing (κ-Routing)"}]},{"id":"blk-95008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158879","text":"Routes queries through knowledge graphs using topological structure, not just embedding similarity. The κ parameter balances exploitation (κ=0, follow strong edges) vs exploration (κ→∞, random walk). Inspired by prefrontal cortex working memory gating."}]},{"id":"blk-95009","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158880","text":"OS-003: Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-95010","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158881","text":"Multi-agent consensus through structured phases: bid → debate → vote → commit. Uses weighted bipolar argumentation, Raft fast-path for agreement, PBFT for Byzantine tolerance, and reputation-weighted bid credibility. Maps to Kahneman's System 2."}]},{"id":"blk-95011","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158882","text":"OS-004: Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-95012","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158883","text":"Three-phase proactive attention cycle — survey (scan all sources, produce salience map) → triage (rank by urgency/novelty/goals) → dispatch (route to pipelines). Runs continuously with adaptive frequency. Grounded in endogenous top-down attention."}]},{"id":"blk-95013","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158884","text":"OS-005: Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-95014","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158885","text":"Graduated model selection across three tiers: "},{"id":"spn-158886","marks":["code"],"text":"local_small"},{"id":"spn-158887","text":" (1B–3B), "},{"id":"spn-158888","marks":["code"],"text":"local_large"},{"id":"spn-158889","text":" (7B–14B), "},{"id":"spn-158890","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud_frontier"},{"id":"spn-158891","text":" (70B+/API). Escalates when confidence falls below threshold; de-escalates by caching successful patterns as procedures. Based on resource rationality theory."}]},{"id":"blk-95015","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158892","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-95016","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158893","text":"The only protocol OpenSentience implements directly. Deny-by-default permissions, five lifecycle states (installed → enabled → running → disabled → removed), three autonomy levels (observe / advise / act), append-only audit trail. ETS-backed lookups at microsecond latency. Ships as the "},{"id":"spn-158894","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-158895","text":" hex package."}]},{"id":"blk-95017","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158896","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-95018","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158897","text":"Defense against prompt injection, model poisoning, side-channel attacks, identity spoofing, and resource exhaustion. Specification-stage protocol."}]},{"id":"blk-95019","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158898","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-95020","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158899","text":"Pipeline enforcement above governance. Two enforced pipelines (reactive: "},{"id":"spn-158900","marks":["code"],"text":"query → recall → topology → deliberate → store"},{"id":"spn-158901","text":"; sprint: planner → generator → evaluator → commit). Quality gates with adversarial grading. Sprint contracts with acceptance criteria. Context management with 60% utilization threshold. Grounded in Norman & Shallice's Supervisory Attentional System."}]},{"id":"blk-95021","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158902","text":"OS-009: PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-95022","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158903","marks":["bold"],"text":"Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory."},{"id":"spn-158904","text":" The first self-improving continual learning benchmark. Measures 9 CL dimensions (retrieval, transfer, uncertainty, feedback integration, forgetting, consolidation, temporal reasoning, multi-agent deliberation, composition). Four-phase evaluation loop: compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose. Features BYOR (Bring Your Own Repo), IRT calibration, three-layer judging, closed-loop verification, leaderboards, and actionable diagnostics."}]},{"id":"blk-95023","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158905","text":"OS-010: PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-95024","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158906","marks":["bold"],"text":"Protocol for Uniform Loop State Exchange."},{"id":"spn-158907","text":" Temporal algebra declaring how loops cycle, nest, and signal. Five canonical phase kinds (retrieve, route, act, learn, consolidate). Six cadence types (event, periodic, streaming, idle, cross_loop_signal, manual). Six canonical cross-loop tokens via CloudEvents v1.0 envelopes ("},{"id":"spn-158908","marks":["code"],"text":"SurpriseSignal"},{"id":"spn-158909","text":" was added in v0.1.1 for GRASP; counted from "},{"id":"spn-158910","marks":["code"],"text":"PULSE/schemas/pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-158911","text":"). BYOL (Bring Your Own Loop) — any system publishing a conforming manifest is automatically PRISM-evaluable."}]},{"id":"blk-95025","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158912","text":"Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-95026","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158913","text":"Governance Shim (OS-006) — OTP Supervision Tree"}]},{"id":"blk-95027","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OpenSentience.Application\n├── OpenSentience.PermissionEngine     (GenServer + ETS — deny-by-default policy)\n├── OpenSentience.AuditWriter          (GenServer — batched append-only)\n├── OpenSentience.AutonomyController   (GenServer + ETS — observe/advise/act)\n├── OpenSentience.AgentSupervisor      (DynamicSupervisor)\n│   ├── AgentLifecycle \"agent-001\"     (GenStateMachine → wraps real process)\n│   ├── AgentLifecycle \"agent-002\"\n│   └── ...\n├── OpenSentience.MCP.Server           (Hermes MCP — governance tools)\n└── OpenSentience.Telemetry            (telemetry handler)"},{"id":"blk-95028","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158914","text":"Triple-Loop Nesting"}]},{"id":"blk-95029","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158915","text":"The reference [&] ecosystem operates with three nested closed loops:"}]},{"id":"blk-95030","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM (outer)              compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose\n  │\n  └─ Graphonomous         retrieve → route → act → learn → consolidate\n       │\n       └─ Deliberation    survey → triage → dispatch → act → learn"},{"id":"blk-95031","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158916","text":"PULSE manifests encode this nesting declaratively."}]},{"id":"blk-95032","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158917","text":"Cognitive Science Grounding"}]},{"id":"blk-95033","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158918","text":"Every protocol maps to published research:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-95035","spans":[{"id":"spn-158919","text":"Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-95036","spans":[{"id":"spn-158920","text":"Theory"}]},{"id":"blk-95037","spans":[{"id":"spn-158921","text":"Key Reference"}]}],"id":"blk-95034","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-95038","spans":[{"id":"spn-158922","text":"OS-001"}]},{"id":"blk-95039","spans":[{"id":"spn-158923","text":"Hippocampal consolidation"}]},{"id":"blk-95040","spans":[{"id":"spn-158924","text":"McClelland et al. 1995"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95041","spans":[{"id":"spn-158925","text":"OS-002"}]},{"id":"blk-95042","spans":[{"id":"spn-158926","text":"Working memory gating"}]},{"id":"blk-95043","spans":[{"id":"spn-158927","text":"O'Reilly & Frank 2006"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95044","spans":[{"id":"spn-158928","text":"OS-003"}]},{"id":"blk-95045","spans":[{"id":"spn-158929","text":"Dual-process theory"}]},{"id":"blk-95046","spans":[{"id":"spn-158930","text":"Kahneman 2011"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95047","spans":[{"id":"spn-158931","text":"OS-004"}]},{"id":"blk-95048","spans":[{"id":"spn-158932","text":"Endogenous attention"}]},{"id":"blk-95049","spans":[{"id":"spn-158933","text":"Desimone & Duncan 1995"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95050","spans":[{"id":"spn-158934","text":"OS-005"}]},{"id":"blk-95051","spans":[{"id":"spn-158935","text":"Resource rationality"}]},{"id":"blk-95052","spans":[{"id":"spn-158936","text":"Lieder & Griffiths 2020"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95053","spans":[{"id":"spn-158937","text":"OS-006"}]},{"id":"blk-95054","spans":[{"id":"spn-158938","text":"Executive function"}]},{"id":"blk-95055","spans":[{"id":"spn-158939","text":"Miyake et al. 2000"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95056","spans":[{"id":"spn-158940","text":"OS-007"}]},{"id":"blk-95057","spans":[{"id":"spn-158941","text":"Immune system analogy"}]},{"id":"blk-95058","spans":[{"id":"spn-158942","text":"—"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95059","spans":[{"id":"spn-158943","text":"OS-008"}]},{"id":"blk-95060","spans":[{"id":"spn-158944","text":"Supervisory attentional system"}]},{"id":"blk-95061","spans":[{"id":"spn-158945","text":"Norman & Shallice 1986"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95062","spans":[{"id":"spn-158946","text":"OS-009"}]},{"id":"blk-95063","spans":[{"id":"spn-158947","text":"Meta-cognition + IRT"}]},{"id":"blk-95064","spans":[{"id":"spn-158948","text":"Signal detection theory"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95065","spans":[{"id":"spn-158949","text":"OS-010"}]},{"id":"blk-95066","spans":[{"id":"spn-158950","text":"Closed-loop control + temporal cognition"}]},{"id":"blk-95067","spans":[{"id":"spn-158951","text":"Wiener 1948"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-95068","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158952","text":"Empirical Results (OS-E001)"}]},{"id":"blk-95069","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158953","text":"Benchmark of Graphonomous v0.3.3 on the full [&] portfolio (18,165 files across 14 projects):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-95071","spans":[{"id":"spn-158954","text":"Metric"}]},{"id":"blk-95072","spans":[{"id":"spn-158955","text":"Result"}]}],"id":"blk-95070","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-95073","spans":[{"id":"spn-158956","text":"QA proxy accuracy (LongMemEval, 500 questions)"}]},{"id":"blk-95074","spans":[{"id":"spn-158957","text":"92.6%"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95075","spans":[{"id":"spn-158958","text":"Session hit rate"}]},{"id":"blk-95076","spans":[{"id":"spn-158959","text":"98.7%"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95077","spans":[{"id":"spn-158960","text":"Mean retrieval latency"}]},{"id":"blk-95078","spans":[{"id":"spn-158961","text":"1.4s"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95079","spans":[{"id":"spn-158962","text":"F1 gain from graph-expanded retrieval vs flat"}]},{"id":"blk-95080","spans":[{"id":"spn-158963","text":"+0.024"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95081","spans":[{"id":"spn-158964","text":"Recall gain from graph-expanded retrieval"}]},{"id":"blk-95082","spans":[{"id":"spn-158965","text":"+0.103"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95083","spans":[{"id":"spn-158966","text":"Automated edges extracted"}]},{"id":"blk-95084","spans":[{"id":"spn-158967","text":"12,871"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95085","spans":[{"id":"spn-158968","text":"Naturally occurring SCCs"}]},{"id":"blk-95086","spans":[{"id":"spn-158969","text":"22 (max κ=27)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95087","spans":[{"id":"spn-158970","text":"κ detection accuracy"}]},{"id":"blk-95088","spans":[{"id":"spn-158971","text":"100% at 27K-node scale"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95089","spans":[{"id":"spn-158972","text":"Test pass rate"}]},{"id":"blk-95090","spans":[{"id":"spn-158973","text":"455/455 (100%)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95091","spans":[{"id":"spn-158974","text":"Consolidation throughput"}]},{"id":"blk-95092","spans":[{"id":"spn-158975","text":"~27.1M nodes/sec"}]}],[{"id":"blk-95093","spans":[{"id":"spn-158976","text":"Abstention accuracy (learned ANN threshold)"}]},{"id":"blk-95094","spans":[{"id":"spn-158977","text":"96.7%"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-95095","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158978","text":"Full results: "},{"id":"spn-158979","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"}],"text":"`docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md`"}]},{"id":"blk-95096","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-158980","text":"κ Proof"}]},{"id":"blk-95097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158981","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"kappa_proof.js"}],"text":"`kappa_proof.js`"},{"id":"spn-158982","text":" is a browser-runnable proof verifying the κ-routing theorem across "},{"id":"spn-158983","marks":["bold"],"text":"1,926,351 test cases"},{"id":"spn-158984","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-95098","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95100","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158985","text":"1,052,740 directed graphs (n=2–5): κ(G) > 0 ⟺ β₁(G) > 0 ⟺ nontrivial SCC"}]}],"id":"blk-95099","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95102","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158986","text":"873,611 finite dynamical systems (n=2–7): κ(f) > 0 ⟺ periodic orbit (period > 1)"}]}],"id":"blk-95101","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-95104","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-158987","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero counterexamples"}]}],"id":"blk-95103","kind":"li